{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1046619-enigmas-skill","id":1046619,"title":"Enigmas Skill","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness"],"posts":[{"date":"2017-02-09T21:38:58-08:00","id":1046619,"title":"Enigmas Skill","content":"Have any of you used this skill in a historic campaign? If so, how did it work out?<br /> <br /> \u200bPersonally I have never liked the skill or understood it. It does nothing for me that other skills such as Investigation and Politics can't do. It almost feels like something the developers put there as a filler, just to have the same number of skills per category. Religion, Travel and Warfare (while also overlapping a lot with existing skills) seem like much more interesting and viable skills for a historical campaign.<br /> <br /> \u200bI would love to be proven wrong however, or at least listen to other opinions on the matter!<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9849-aristarkos","name":"Aristarkos","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9849_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"369"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-09T21:52:53-08:00","id":1046627,"title":"","content":"It's a skill for encrypting and decrypting codes and cyphers, basically. A more accurate name for it would probably be Cryptography, but it's presumably named for <a href=\"https://en.m.wikipedia.org/wiki/Enigma_machine\" target=\"_blank\">the enigma machine</a>. Which makes sense as a precursor to Computers, as computers are, at their most basic function, tools for encoding and decoding information. Enigmas is simply the skill for manually doing what we now use computers to do.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-09T22:32:32-08:00","id":1046641,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1046619-enigmas-skill?p=1046627#post1046627\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It's a skill for encrypting and decrypting codes and cyphers, basically. A more accurate name for it would probably be Cryptography, but it's presumably named for <a href=\"https://en.m.wikipedia.org/wiki/Enigma_machine\" target=\"_blank\">the enigma machine</a>. Which makes sense as a precursor to Computers, as computers are, at their most basic function, tools for encoding and decoding information. Enigmas is simply the skill for manually doing what we now use computers to do.</div> </div> </div> </div>\u200bI have always used Investigation as the logic-heavy skill for finding patterns and cracking any type of mystery or riddle, including cryptography. I suppose many Storytellers don't, though.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9849-aristarkos","name":"Aristarkos","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9849_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"369"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}